WEBVTT

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.890
Are you all right?

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.500
All right, of course I'm all right.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.040
These people who need help, my help.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.000
Read this. It's a...

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.980
It's a rejection. Another slap in the face

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.060
from those myopic idiots at the academy.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.590
The article proves we can finally harness DNA.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:29.970
The implications are...

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.990
And what is their response?

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.720
Put your hand.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.200
What?

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:35.970
Oh, leave me alone, Graham.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.500
Oh, Graham, why do I bother?

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.320
Charity, my patience, my vision.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.310
They're wasted on these feckless morons.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.860
Tortured to have my genius ignored like this.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:56.670
Why do they do it, Graham?

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:58.830
Is it envy?

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.050
Is it stupidity? What?

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:07.160
I don't give a damn.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.980
You don't give a damn.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:11.000
it is what i am i was once a man i know the evil men do do not bring your evil here

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:26.720
i warn you beware the wrath of one thing there's someone here to see you go away an editor for modern

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.870
science magazine turn the buzz off

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.400
Can't you see I'm busy?

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.020
Dr. Arcane, I presume.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.550
I'm Catherine St. James from Modern Science.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.970
I was hoping we'd not be able to arrange an interview,

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.810
but if this is a bad time...

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.710
Oh, bad time. Nonsense. Wonderful time.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.750
We always make time for members of the press.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:51.890
Graham, the young lady's bags.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.290
Oh, no need, doctor. I'm fine.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.330
Graham? Charmed. I didn't quite catch your name.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.190
Your hand.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:02:59.980
Oh, it's not.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.050
Nothing. It's a minor accident.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.380
I can't tell you what a pleasure it is to finally meet you.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.360
But I must admit, I'm a bit surprised.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.260
How so?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.860
Somehow I expected a much older man.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.350
I mean, knowing the myriad of contributions you've made to the field of genetic engineering.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.950
No, most of my work is considered theoretical.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.480
Your entropic theory of DNA mutation already has practical application.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:29.970
Well, for a reporter, you seem surprisingly well-versed.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.240
in such an esoteric subject.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.300
I'm full of surprises, Doctor.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.140
I also have a degree in microbiology

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:40.530
and a natural fascination with arcane knowledge.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:43.370
Jolly good.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:03.960
St. James.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:04.620
Catherine.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:05.900
Catherine.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.590
Not that I'm in the least bit put out,

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.340
but I'm a little curious to know why you didn't phone for an appointment first.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.960
Would you have said yes?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:15.970
Of course not.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.560
You would have turned me away before even meeting me.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.680
What an unfortunate mistake that would have been.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.620
I find that being a little aggressive helps me get what I want.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.200
And in this case, what I want is you.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:29.960
Forgive me, but I...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.470
I find that a little hard to believe.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:37.580
I've read your work. Bold. Dangerously original.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.520
And I wondered if the man would be the same.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.220
I thought you'd make an effective counterpoint

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.400
all the stuffed shirts I've covered in the past.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:50.860
Well, no mere interview would ever convince those intimidated by my work.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.460
This would be your chance to be heard by everyone in a national journal.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:59.230
And frankly, it would be cool for me to interview a brilliant and controversial figure.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:08.410
I promise you'll find the procedure both quick and painful, or long and pleasurable.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.970
Yes, indeed. You really do understand, don't you?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.220
Not until you explained it to me.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.450
Careful. This pipe's filled with power.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.560
Dangerous radioactive chemical toxins

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.240
have stripped the skin right off this pretty little hand.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.930
Some things are just better left alone.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.120
In a very...

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.800
...interview would be complete, would it?

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:59.580
Without getting to know the man behind the work, Graham?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.640
Miss St. James will be staying with us.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:05.720
Let's try to make her very comfortable, shall we?

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:12.870
Is everything prepared?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.340
Well, sir, isn't it a little bit suspicious

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.260
how she just dropped in from nowhere,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.470
then consented to stay?

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.620
What, are you, worried that Miss St. James

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.100
is planning to use me, Grave?

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.810
Well, yes.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.610
Stimulating thought, isn't it?

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.200
Graham, you must have been teased by a beautiful young woman at one time in your life.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.140
Obviously not.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:08.150
I must say, everything about this day has been impressive.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:09.970
And most unexpected.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:15.190
Leading me to wonder why this particularly attractive woman has chosen to grace my home.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.910
She has reasons she'd rather keep private for now.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.760
Just as long as she makes them known sooner or later.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.950
Anton, what do you dream about?

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:35.170
Well, mostly my work. I'm hoping you'll change all that.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.800
Are you trying to make me blush?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.650
You're very beautiful and intelligent.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:44.020
You understand my work, most of all.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.290
You're a woman of mystery.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.510
Everything about you tantalizes.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:56.450
You shouldn't, really.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.970
I mean, I'd love to, but I'm a journalist on a...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.000
assignment.

00:08:01.244 --> 00:08:04.124
And my professional ethics will allow me to mix business with pleasure.

00:08:05.052 --> 00:08:05.892
Oh.

00:08:07.036 --> 00:08:09.036
scruples

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.660
to the power of revenge.

00:09:19.004 --> 00:09:19.404
Certainly.

00:09:19.612 --> 00:09:21.072
You have been a busy boy.

00:09:26.652 --> 00:09:28.652
a shame

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.430
Oops! How clumsy of me.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:53.710
Thank you.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:22.250
hurt good come on there's something i want to show you do you like it thought the place could

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:28.880
use a woman's touch d fool you've destroyed a life's work

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.140
My work.

00:10:32.588 --> 00:10:33.968
Take years to replace it.

00:10:34.048 --> 00:10:35.188
You're overreacting.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.600
Paid you to do this.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:38.900
Please, Anton.

00:10:39.628 --> 00:10:40.348
This is strict.

00:10:41.004 --> 00:10:41.504
personally.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:07.960
arcane

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:45.820
will do fine.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.440
We'll have a nice view from here.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:55.840
What you're getting yourself into.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.920
Shut up, Arcane, and enjoy the show.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.770
Everything you love is just over there.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:11.670
The explosion should take out your home, lab, and your pathetic little ego.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:15.360
The wonders of modern technology.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:47.980
your pathetic life's work, and the next step is to deal with you.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.240
With what?

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.640
You're no more a threat to me than that puny explosion.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:58.920
This obviously isn't real. Just look around you. Fascinating.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.740
taste, feeling. All the senses seem to be working, and yet something is wrong. Very wrong.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:22.190
The thing from the swamp. You've angered him by blowing the chemical dump and poisoning

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.190
his habitat. He's come for you.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:21.010
Sunderland Arcane, General Sunderland's daughter, killed him.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.080
And now you're going to die.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:29.960
This is our...

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.130
Absolutely amazing.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.710
I don't know how you did that, but believe me, Arcane, I'll kill you yet.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.860
You murdered the kindest, most honorable man I've known.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:43.030
General Sunderland was a duplicitous swine and a blight on humanity.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.470
Do you know anything about your dear daddy's accomplishments?

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.770
Biological warfare, death devices, assassination.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.720
He even created mutant children to work in a gold mine in Brazil.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.420
Well, he left you quite a legacy to live up to.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:04.040
He was a great man, a businessman and philanthropist.

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.840
Philanthropist? Don't make me laugh.

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.720
He lived for power and profit.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.010
He was good, maybe even great.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.520
Probably because his mind was as twisted as his body was,

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:14.600
ugly and mutilated.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:15.580
How dare you?

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:19.810
Think about it. Try to remember.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.060
That's not my father.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:28.230
Is he wrong, my dear?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:29.980
Your father?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.440
Father kidnapped my wife for his own sick pleasure.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:36.520
When I found out about it, he tried to kill us both and succeeded in killing her.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:40.520
For that reason alone, I won't be content till I see you with him in hell.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.460
Girls should poke their noses in where they don't belong.

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:00.930
Toxic.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:04.640
Toxic.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.020
These chemicals could kill more than just the swamp.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:10.950
Don't stop them.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.190
They could poison the environment of this whole area.

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:16.470
Generations to come.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.410
I don't think it's going to be...

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.250
Green horde creature.

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:02.680
Oh, him.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.840
You don't want to worry about him.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:07.260
It's me you'll want to worry about.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:11.080
No, your father had a magic way with the blade.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.060
Justify his murder with pathetic lies.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.060
I knew him.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:16.290
His daughter.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.080
I find this strangely amusing.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.530
Your father never even mentioned he had a daughter.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.000
War came first.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.460
I learned to live with that.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.880
After the work he always found time to be with me.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:08.530
You took away what time he would have had left!

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.350
Save your sentimental bromides, my dear.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.040
Doesn't become ill.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:14.440
What now?

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:19.780
It's your pretty throat.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.380
the consequences and now you're gonna have to suffer the consequences of your actions

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:27.700
honey just business that's my little girl

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.290
Why not, girl?

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:22.400
Wait, I knew you were behind all this.

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:25.670
What is it, one of your ridiculous morality lessons?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.860
This was not your lesson to learn.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.980
Good, and kindly put it.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:44.330
to stop to all this ridiculous charade i wanted to destroy everything you loved before i killed

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:52.260
you that would be too easy too simple better that you suffer never knowing when or how the

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:59.200
end will come for you no it will come eventually

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:03.160
from one victim of your madness or another.
